DS2 Save Manager
Copyright 2026 Mert

This project builds on the work of others:

- darthdemono/sl2-analyzer (https://github.com/darthdemono/sl2-analyzer), Apache License 2.0,
  Copyright 2026 Jubair Hasan (DarthDemono).
  Used: the db_ds2 item tables (flattened into src-tauri/data/items.json by
  scripts/build-item-db.mjs, with shields split into their own category and armour slots added),
  the finding that both Dark Souls II releases share one save layout, character field offsets
  (class, covenant, gender, hollowing, deaths, play time in the title record), and the derived-stat
  curves ported to src/game.ts.

- alfizari/Dark-Souls-2-Save-Editor-PS4-PC (https://github.com/alfizari/Dark-Souls-2-Save-Editor-PS4-PC),
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 Ahmed.
  Used as the reference for the SL2 entry layout, the Scholar of the First Sin key, the name,
  souls, attribute and inventory offsets, and default durabilities for new inventory records.
  Its decrypted sample save is used, outside the repository, for local tests.

- TKGP/SoulsFormats (https://github.com/JKAnderson/SoulsFormats): the two AES-128 save keys
  (SFUtil.GetDS2SaveKey and SFUtil.GetScholarSaveKey), which ship inside the games.

- The menu font (src/public/fonts/ds2-menu.woff2) is traced from the bitmap font atlas that Dark
  Souls II itself ships (font/*/FeFont_Big.fontbnd.dcx) by scripts/build-game-font.py. The glyph
  designs belong to their owners (FromSoftware / Bandai Namco); the file is kept for this private
  project only. EB Garamond and Cinzel (SIL Open Font License) are bundled as fallbacks.

